{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518122-v20-shifting-clan-weaknesses-around","id":1518122,"title":"[V20] Shifting Clan Weaknesses Around","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-15T19:31:42-07:00","id":1518122,"title":"[V20] Shifting Clan Weaknesses Around","content":"While I was cycling today, I got to thinking about the Followers of Set Clan weakness.<br /> <br /> Namely that a hypersensitivity/vulnerability to light really works better as a Lasombra weakness. What with them being the &quot;Clan of Shadows&quot; and all. That they cast no reflection is not without logic, but less logic than just having the Setite weakness instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Once I got on that train of thought, it occurred to me that another Clan could probably do well with the &quot;No Reflections&quot; weakness: Clan Toreador. The existing Toreador Clan weakness has always been one difficult to run, as it depends wholly on the ST + Player remembering it exists and role-playing it. Where it's either debilitating or nonexistent, so you have to work extra hard threading the needle. It's less concrete and mechanistic than &quot;Is Ugly&quot; or &quot;Can Only Feed From [X]&quot;, more fluid and context-dependent.<br /> <br /> Whereas Toreador without reflections would sort of play into the Clan's vanity. For a Clan (culturally) obsessed with beauty, that they can't easily see beauty in themselves would make for a sore spot. With the Lasombra, there's the question over whether most would care about not seeing themselves. (Them having frustrated vanity does come up, but only rarely. They're more about Power.). It seemed more like an extra bit tacked onto the Clan of Shadows because someone had to represent the &quot;No Reflections&quot; side of vampire myths, and all the Camarilla Clans were already taken.<br /> <br /> Toreador that cast no reflection would need to lean all the more on connections to other people. Ghouls or the like to pretty them up and flatter their vanity. And Clanmates to get an &quot;objective&quot; view on (albeit one with the inevitable prospect of spite or dishonesty). Moreover, since they can't take beauty from their own unchanging, immortal form, finding it in other things/people is all the more vital.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Circling back around to the Setites, we need to then decide what their weakness will be in absence of a light sensitivity. What immediately came to mind is to lean into the Clan's serpent associations: make them cold blooded.<br /> <br /> Obviously, all vampires are room-temperature corpses, and thus usually have cold blood. Rather, it means, like a reptile, the Followers of Set become lethargic in the presence of chill. Increasing penalties to dice pools proportional to cold.<br /> <br /> This can be mitigated in a couple ways. <b>First</b> by simply moving to a place with warmer ambient temperature or huddling next to something warmer in the environment (like a radiator). <b>Second</b> by using some kind of heat-generating personal effect, like an electric blanket or thermal patch. <b>Third</b> by wearing lots of layers, which (because they don't generate heat) can slow down heat loss but not stop it (so the Setite in cold weather needs to get their business done quickly). <b>Fourth</b> by remaining in close contact with one or more living bodies, which synergizes well with their Presence and Social primaries. F<b>ifth</b>, having recently consumed blood (the warmth persists for a time, especially with layers keeping it in). And <b>sixth</b> by just living in places with warm or temperate climates, which handily reinforces why Setites would prefer living in the Mediterranean or other places snakes like to live.<br /> <br /> All inconvenient, as vampire weaknesses should be. But workable. Especially if your whole deal is being crafty, social, and good at networking.<br /> <br /> I also like the mental image of Hesha Ruhadze sticking a bunch of thermal patches and long underwear under his suit, to keep warm during the winter when he can't retreat to the tropics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T01:14:33-07:00","id":1518132,"title":"","content":"Those are nice ideas. Though I'd give Setites the usual Toreador weakness of fixation; it makes the Toreador-Lasombra-Setite switches a nice full circle, and feeds into the Dark Gnosticism of Setites that the material world is a prison/trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T05:58:38-07:00","id":1518237,"title":"","content":"I don't know, to me it seems kind of weak, unless he already lives in a cold place by nature it's a weakness that doesn't cause problems most of the time, I don't think it's a bad idea, but it's not practical and looks much more like a defect. The Setites' original weakness may be odd, but mechanically functional in any place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T04:45:56-07:00","id":1518424,"title":"","content":"My pun-inflicted headcanon is that Setites got their weakness because of how <i>shady</i> they are. The running themes with them are literally corruption, drug-dealings and dark cults up to 11.<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, there is a Apep/Python/ Vasuki part of clan identity, with all giant snakes having their grudges against sun deities Ra/Apollo/Garuda. Given Setites fixation on Gnosticism and their blend of all world religions on their quest to resurrect their god, this clan weakness suits them and may prove their point and strengthen their faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28102-stathmin","name":"Stathmin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T16:25:26-07:00","id":1518459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518122-v20-shifting-clan-weaknesses-around?p=1518237#post1518237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, to me it seems kind of weak, unless he already lives in a cold place by nature it's a weakness that doesn't cause problems most of the time, I don't think it's a bad idea, but it's not practical and looks much more like a defect. The Setites' original weakness may be odd, but mechanically functional in any place.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue the same about a number of canon weaknesses. Weak or situational.<br /> <br /> Take the Tzimisce weakness. If they don't have their two fistfuls of &quot;native soil&quot;, they become gradually weaker and more useless, until they can barely function. But if they DO have them while resting, they might as well have no weakness whatsoever. Especially if, like Dracula, the Tzimisce sets up several redundant caches of native soil around town, so they never need worry about going too long without it.<br /> <br /> In that sense, a Setite &quot;cold intolerance&quot; at least requires more work-around. Especially during winter or in naturally cold climates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T16:30:39-07:00","id":1518460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stathmin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518122-v20-shifting-clan-weaknesses-around?p=1518424#post1518424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jokes aside, there is a Apep/Python/ Vasuki part of clan identity, with all giant snakes having their grudges against sun deities Ra/Apollo/Garuda. Given Setites fixation on Gnosticism and their blend of all world religions on their quest to resurrect their god, this clan weakness suits them and may prove their point and strengthen their faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fully aware of the justification given for the canon Setite weakness. Nonetheless, my assertion still stands: the Lasombra - the Clan of Shadows, the Kings &amp; Queens of Darkness - have a far greater thematic claim on light sensitivity. Versus the Followers of Set, whose proprietary Discipline makes them snake-like.<br /> <br /> Again, I contend the Lasombra WOULD have light sensitivity, if White Wolf hadn't used them to check the &quot;no reflection&quot; box on the list of vampire tropes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T17:10:48-07:00","id":1518463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518122-v20-shifting-clan-weaknesses-around?p=1518459#post1518459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One could argue the same about a number of canon weaknesses. Weak or situational.<br /> <br /> Take the Tzimisce weakness. If they don't have their two fistfuls of &quot;native soil&quot;, they become gradually weaker and more useless, until they can barely function. But if they DO have them while resting, they might as well have no weakness whatsoever. Especially if, like Dracula, the Tzimisce sets up several redundant caches of native soil around town, so they never need worry about going too long without it.<br /> <br /> In that sense, a Setite &quot;cold intolerance&quot; at least requires more work-around. Especially during winter or in naturally cold climates.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Tzimisce, it is more functional than the Setite, because if in fact he has to sleep in the soil in which he was born, then his weakness is obvious and it is probably where he sleeps, and he will not have the freedom to sleep where he wants (or when necessary), unless he limits himself to living within his territory or always carries said soil with him, knowing that and I believe it is not a secret at this point, just steal or destroy that soil and you will have an advantage against the tzimice, in the case of the Setite you just take him out of the cold place in question that he will soon recover, recovering the land or returning to it, can be much more terrible, you have a external and explorable weakness and to be honest the whole ministry clan would be well hidden during the winter if it had this weakness and also would limit the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T19:16:54-07:00","id":1518597,"title":"","content":"The Lasombra weakness could work well for the Gangrel. It makes them creatures who keep to the wilds because technology literally won't work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T19:27:09-07:00","id":1518599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518122-v20-shifting-clan-weaknesses-around?p=1518597#post1518597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra weakness could work well for the Gangrel. It makes them creatures who keep to the wilds because technology literally won't work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the classic Lasombra weakness (&quot;no reflection&quot;), or the V5 Lasombra weakness (&quot;bad with technology&quot;)?<br /> <br /> In either event, I kind of like Clan Gangrel's classic weakness still. They're almost beasts of the wild, so giving in to the Beast makes them literally more bestial. There's concordance there that works very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T20:35:59-07:00","id":1518606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518122-v20-shifting-clan-weaknesses-around?p=1518459#post1518459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One could argue the same about a number of canon weaknesses. Weak or situational.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>However to name or call the issue of weaknesses of different Kindred, it has to be noted that every group of Vampires has ideas, culture, means, and attitude to deal and even benefit from their particular weakness.<br /> While a young Vampire Neonate might still be bothered or hindred by these problematic traits, with learning and experience these bothersome conditions can definitely become to at least some meaninggful extent more of a indication related to pride and identity. <br /> <br /> Vampiresses ( and Ghouls, and Revenants ) can also define and distinguish in how exactly,and how effectively, they deal with their particular weakness.<br /> Helping other Kindred in dealing with her or his particular weakness is definitely and certainly a worthy and interesting interest, or field of knowledge, or specialization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}